    <string name="settings_card_access_body">A removable eSIM (eUICC) can let VowiDroid read it and answer authentication over its own channel, the way eSIM manager apps reach it. That keeps working while the SIM is switched off in Android\'s settings, and needs no adb step.\n\nThe card decides. A card without access rules is allowed on phones that follow Android\'s default. A card that carries access rules (ARA-M) must list the SHA-1 of this build\'s signing certificate in them; cards whose owner can edit the rules, such as eSTK.me, take this value:</string>
    <string name="settings_card_access_copy">Copy hash</string>
    <string name="settings_card_access_copied">Hash copied</string>
    <string name="action_close">Close</string>

    <!-- Line settings: device identity (IMEI) -->
    <string name="line_imei_title">Device identity (IMEI)</string>
    <string name="line_imei_body">Some carriers ask the ePDG for the phone\'s IMEI and allow Wi-Fi calling only for devices they know. VowiDroid sends this value when asked, once the ePDG has proven itself, and names the line\'s SIP instance with it. Leave it empty to send none.</string>
